    {
      "id": "c25-l2",
      "title": "Searching a Tree",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "Finding a key works like inserting: compare, and go left or right. Every step throws away a whole subtree, just like binary search throws away half the array.",
        "In a well-balanced tree with a million keys, that's only about 20 steps. Unlike a sorted array, a tree also stays sorted when you add new keys.",
        "The height of a tree (the longest path from the root down) shows how many steps a search can take. If you insert keys that are already sorted, every node goes right, and the tree turns into a long list."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "#include <stdio.h>",
          "#include <stdlib.h>",
          "",
          "typedef struct node {",
          "    int key;",
          "    struct node *left, *right;",
          "} Node;",
          "",
          "Node *insert(Node *t, int key) {",
          "    if (t == NULL) {",
          "        t = malloc(sizeof(Node));",
          "        t->key = key;",
          "        t->left = t->right = NULL;",
          "    } else if (key < t->key)",
          "        t->left = insert(t->left, key);",
          "    else",
          "        t->right = insert(t->right, key);",
          "    return t;",
          "}",
          "",
          "Node *find(Node *t, int key) {",
          "    while (t != NULL && t->key != key)",
          "        t = key < t->key ? t->left : t->right;",
          "    return t;",
          "}",
          "",
          "int height(Node *t) {",
          "    int l, r;",
          "    if (t == NULL) return 0;",
          "    l = height(t->left);",
          "    r = height(t->right);",
          "    return 1 + (l > r ? l : r);",
          "}",
          "",
          "int main() {",
          "    Node *a = NULL, *b = NULL;",
          "    int mixed[] = {4, 2, 6, 1, 3, 5, 7};",
          "    int i;",
          "    for (i = 0; i < 7; i++) {",
          "        a = insert(a, mixed[i]);",
          "        b = insert(b, i + 1);",
          "    }",
          "    printf(\"find 5: %s\\n\", find(a, 5) ? \"yes\" : \"no\");",
          "    printf(\"find 9: %s\\n\", find(a, 9) ? \"yes\" : \"no\");",
          "    printf(\"height: %d and %d\\n\", height(a), height(b));",
          "    return 0;",
          "}"
        ],
        "output": []
      },
